00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:00.960
Let's talk about BigQuery first.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.570
Google BigQuery--
it's now 10 years old.

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:06.360
In June, we celebrated the
10th anniversary of BigQuery.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:09.600
BigQuery has customers
from a few terabytes

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.130
to hundreds of petabytes.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:13.530
It's a completely
serverless technology.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:15.120
What do I mean by that?

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:18.180
Well, it means you don't have to
worry about any infrastructure

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:18.840
pieces.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:21.120
Just bring your data
and start analyzing.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:22.790
Start writing queries on it.

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:23.880
There is no monitoring.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.050
There is no administration.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:27.300
There is no machines.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:28.590
There is no nodes.

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:30.970
There are no servers that
you need to worry about.

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:34.360
So most of that is
managed by Google.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.820
We take care of
all that for you.

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:40.030
The second thing-- we are
highly differentiated.

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:44.250
We provide you capability
to ingest tens of millions

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.890
of events in real
time into BigQuery.

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:50.130
And a lot of
organizations like King,

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:51.600
which is a gaming company--

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.370
they have in-game
events that happen,

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:55.480
and they want to stream
that in real time

00:01:55.480 --> 00:02:00.310
so they can analyze what users
are doing on their platform.

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:03.480
So it's possible-- and many
[INAUDIBLE] large scale

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:04.240
events--

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:09.180
it does not impact your query
performance on top of that data

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:12.195
because we completely
distribute or decouple

00:02:12.195 --> 00:02:15.960
our compute and storage layers.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:18.030
In addition to that, we
have embedded machine

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:19.600
learning capability,
where you can

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:22.650
write SQL commands to create
machine learning models

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:25.020
and get advanced predictions.

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:28.350
And finally, we don't want
insights to be limited

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:30.060
to few in the organization.

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:32.250
We want insights for everyone.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:34.620
We have made a lot of
investment in the space,

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:38.880
but BigQuery is being used by
organizations like AirAsia,

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.400
where they were able to
reduce their operational costs

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.010
in an airline by
5% to 10% by making

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:47.100
those insights available
to everybody in front line

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.160
so that they can make
better decisions.

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:52.500
So those are the key
capabilities that we provide.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.410
One thing that BigQuery
is great at is scale.

00:02:55.410 --> 00:03:00.930
We are really powering some of
the largest of the workloads

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:02.730
in analytics space.

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:06.480
Our largest customer has
more than 350 petabytes

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:08.980
of data in the data warehouse.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:10.920
One of the largest
queries that was run

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.800
was roughly 100
trillion rows that

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:16.240
were queried in a single query.

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:21.930
And now we have seen up to
10,000 concurrent users being

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:23.550
used by one of our customers.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:25.530
So concurrency at
a very high scale

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:28.810
is also supported in a big way.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:31.020
Let's talk about HSBC.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:33.050
It's a systemic bank.

00:03:33.050 --> 00:03:34.740
It's highly regulated.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:37.980
HSBC uses BigQuery to
a lot of large scale

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:42.083
analytics for a lot of
regulatory reporting and all.

00:03:42.083 --> 00:03:43.500
One of the key
things that we were

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:46.680
able to do by
working with HSBC is

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:48.690
provide a lot of
security capabilities

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:50.400
in BigQuery, like CMEK.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.740
That's customer manager
encryption keys.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:54.870
Virtual private connect.

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:56.400
So all of these VPC SC--

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:00.300
all these capabilities
we built with HSBC.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.890
They are proven.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:05.370
They're used by some of the
largest banks in the world.

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:08.820
In HSBC's case, they bring
data from 40 plus countries--

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:10.340
all transaction data--

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:13.540
they put it into their
data lake/data warehouse.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:16.589
With BigQuery they
analyze all of this data,

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:18.089
and at the end of
the day, they have

00:04:18.089 --> 00:04:23.640
to report to regulators about
the viability of the business

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:25.160
based on all this data.

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:27.360
And all of this is running
in few minutes, which

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:30.770
used to take like, I think, 30
hours on PREM systems and stuff

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:31.270
like that.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:33.353
And you have to do this
every day, so at 30 hours,

00:04:33.353 --> 00:04:36.220
you cannot go out
and report every day.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:38.890
So on BigQuery, we can
do it in a few minutes,

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:41.210
and it's allowing
them to scale--

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:44.038
to scale their business.

00:04:44.038 --> 00:04:46.580
TINO TERESHKO: So BigQuery is
much more than a data warehouse

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:48.990
because we have so much
advanced capabilities,

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:52.590
